vides a concrete emptiness check while keeping existing-database changes on the already agreed migration path.","recommended":"Use EnsureCreated only when the database has no tables; otherwise leave schema changes to the reviewed deployment migration.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"How should startup determine whether a database qualifies for EnsureCreated, given that existing databases must use the reviewed deployment migration?","uncertainty":3}],"checks":{"critic":[{"finding":"AC-9.1 says a stock request filtered to an out-of-scope warehouse returns 403, but AC-1.2 says scoped collection calls return a list limited to the caller's scope and the supplied filters, which implies 200 with an empty or filtered list.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-9.1 relies on a `warehouseId` query filter for the stock collection, but no anchor shows that parameter in the contract; the anchored warehouse collection (listReceipts) takes only Search, Status, DateFrom and DateTo.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-9.2 expects 403 for another organization's order, but the contract describes getCustomerOrder as 'scoped to the authenticated customer' and declares a 404, and the spec gives no reason for choosing 403 over 404.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-9 says callers are authorized by 'PostgreSQL account roles and scopes', but no role-to-operation permission table is given or anchored in the contract (AC-9.1 just says 'the role permitted for stock listing'), so the 403 behaviour of most operations is undefined.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-9 and AC-9.6 rely on 'enabled' and 'disabled' accounts, but the anchored AccountInput schema has no status or enabled field and no anchor shows how an account becomes disabled.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-9.4 assumes a 'contract-defined password-setting operation', but none is anchored; the only anchored customer-auth operation is signInCustomer.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-9.2 needs 'a valid one-time code available for that account', but the spec never says how the code is delivered or how a test can get it through a public surface, so the AC cannot be run as written.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-2.1, AC-2.4, AC-2.5, AC-5.1 and AC-9.4 are checked by reading database rows or table lists directly, not through an API response.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-2 uses EnsureCreated for empty databases and reviewed migrations for existing ones, but EnsureCreated writes no migrations-history table, so a database it creates cannot later take a migration; the spec also never defines 'genuinely empty' or how startup detects it, even though Program.cs currently calls EnsureCreated every time.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":6,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-2.3 covers only changing an order before packing; there is no AC for the contract's 409 when an order is already packed, or for createReceipt's declared 409 conflict.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-7.1 expects the authorization URL in a response field named `message` (AC-7.3 just says 'the response field'), but no anchor shows that field in the operation's response schema.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-7 depends on 'the organization's existing staff identity provider', but the spec never names it and no anchor shows it exists, so the token-validation settings it requires cannot be identified.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-3.1 only checks that GET / returns 200 with Seed:Demo=true, which would pass even if SeedData.Run never ran or inserted nothing.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-4 and AC-4.1 depend on ASM-1 (two to five rows per table), but the accepted assumptions list is empty,